    "narrative": "The July 4th slate sees **Corbin Carroll** (74.49) and **Brice Turang** (73.40) anchor our lineup as the premier plays of the day. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a prime order spot and a favorable matchup against Woodruff, compounded by the slow delivery of the opposition, which creates an ideal environment for his elite speed to generate stolen base value. Similarly, **Brice Turang** earns top billing due to a high-upside matchup against Me. Kelly; his 10% order bonus combined with a significant +19% bump from the starter's skill profile makes him a core engine for our daily production. **Josh Naylor** also stands out with a 71.12 score, leveraging the same advantageous matchup against Bieber to drive our power categories.\n\nOur lineup construction emphasizes efficiency, forcing a difficult bench decision regarding **Travis Bazzana** (48.89). Despite a respectable score boosted by an order-one lead-off spot, **Travis Bazzana** narrowly missed the cut because the density of high-floor options in our middle infield and utility slots\u2014specifically **Kyle Karros**, who carries a 63.92 score thanks to a massive +14% park factor and platoon advantage against Ray\u2014provided a higher mathematical expectation. We are also closely monitoring the utility of **James Wood** (52.66); while his xwOBA of .418 is elite, the risk posed by the opposing catcher\u2019s 1.89s pop time tempers his potential for stolen bases, keeping him in the starting lineup but strictly as an efficiency play rather than a primary speed catalyst.\n\nWe remain cautious regarding **Austin Riley** (52.57), whose projection is hindered by a slightly tougher matchup against Manaea. While he remains above our 50-point start threshold, he lacks the platoon-driven ceiling of **Kyle Karros** or **Seiya Suzuki** (65.20). With **Vinnie Pasquantino** and **Tyler Soderstrom** remaining on the IL, we are limited in our ability to rotate for late-game defensive substitutions, increasing our reliance on the health and performance of the current active starters. No major weather concerns have been flagged for today's venues, but the reliance on **Dalton Rushing** (47.03) against a lefty like Peralta remains our primary risk point; his platoon disadvantage is mitigated only by the starter's 4.54 xERA, making him a marginal start we will be monitoring closely for potential pinch-hit substitution if the game turns late.",
